content.text:
Desktop looks good, but the ground is very dark because the wash and vignette. Fine. The map width at desktop shows train centered and depot. It's sparse but playable. "Improve how the map looks" - the biomes are distinct. 

However, in the valley screenshot, the tree canopies are dark green circles with barely visible trunks. Fine.

One issue: The train appears tiny on desktop because PPM fixed and viewport wide; the camera vertical focus .6 means train at 60%? Actually train center around y=450 of 900, fine. The player is on deck.

Now, the biome HUD top-left is tiny on desktop (9.5px) but readable. Fine.

Now check mobile with workshop badge etc. no need.

Need ensure `?shot=deck` still renders with new biome (at y=0 valley). In debug `shot=deck`, train.moving=true and sim 90 -> moves ~157px, still valley. Good.

Check `?shot=win` and `dead` render correctly with GOAL 5000. `dead` sets y=-1370m -> badlands (since 1000-2000), nice. Win sets 5000 -> ash.

But `showOverlay('win')` calls closeBuild, sets overlay; okay.

Now, the map improvement could include occasional biome boundary markers/gates so the player knows they're entering. The banner covers. Maybe add a large arch sign at each 1000m boundary? That would look nice and reinforce transitions. The requirement: "make it sure they blend well together as you transition". A gate might conflict with "blend" (hard boundary marker). But the banner does it. Maybe add roadside signs at boundaries showing biome names? Could be a nice touch, but not necessary.

Potential bug: `biomeIdxAt` at exactly m=0? returns valley. `S.biomeIdx` initialized 0. If the train starts at y=0 and moves, no banner until 1000. Good.

Potential bug: `S.biomeIdx` tracks backward (if train somehow moves backward, no). Player walking away doesn't affect. Fine.

Potential issue: if the game is reset after winning at 5000, chunks generated but reset doesn't regenerate props or reset biome-specific generated state? Props still there, fine. `S.biomeIdx=0`. The train at y=0. Banner removed. Good.

Potential issue: `S.train.y` in reset sets 0 but `S.cam` reset 0. Fine.

Now, we changed `S.train` in reset to a new object; `S.biomeIdx` set separately. Good.

Test stress run perhaps. We should run a long simulation to catch biome-specific drawing errors across 5000m and transitions. The previous stress script no longer exists. Let's create a stress test that simulates at 60fps with draw? Drawing in headless is costly but we can call update and draw each frame? The existing game loop handles. Better use page evaluate to step update across all biomes and call draw occasionally, and check for exceptions. Also screenshot at random points.

Let's run a simulation from 0 to 5000, stepping update at 1/60, forcing fuel, and calling draw every 60 frames. Since code uses canvas transforms, draw works. Catch errors. Also measure max props and performance.

Write stress-biomes.cjs:
```js
await page.goto(base); page.click('#go');
const res = await page.evaluate(() => {
 S.mode='play';
 let err=null; let yStart=S.train.y;
 // build workshop, etc.
 for(let i=0;i<40000;i++){
   if(S.train.fuel<40) S.train.fuel=80;
   if(i%600===0) draw();
   try{update(1/60);}catch(e){err=...;break;}
   if(S.mode!=='play') S.mode='play';
   if(S.train.y < -GOAL_M*PPM) break;
 }
 return {...}
});
```
But `update` at high speed will pass 5000 and win -> showOverlay. We reset mode to play each iteration and break when y past goal. But update sets mode win; we can count. Better stop when reaching goal. If mode becomes win, break and record.

Also draw every 60 frames at various biomes. Need not move player. Train moving. Fuel top-ups. The train will hit zombies/debris but fuel forced.

Check `S.amb` count, props counts. Also maybe `chunks.size`. Let's do.

